Lets a toplevel of the embedder's on Chromium's Wayland connection, such as the app's Settings
window, compose through a browser window's input method. The compositor gives a client's input
method to its text inputs, and Chromium's one zwp_text_input_v3 drops an enter for a surface that
isn't Chromium's. The embedder names the surface and the window it composes through
(WaylandProxy::SetEmbedderTextInputSurface); an enter for that surface gives that window
text-input focus, so its input method enables for the client the core gives it, without making the
window active, as the embedder's surface has the keys. Keys are untouched: Chromium still drops
those for a surface that isn't its own. Removing the window ends the entry, and the embedder ends it
before destroying the surface. Hooks only: the logic is in browser_core/platform/linux/.
